---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | SSEGU"
  description="How SSEGU handles information about visitors and submissions."
>
  <div class="shell prose-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>Last updated: 16 November 2026.</strong> This notice explains how SSEGU handles
      information when you use the SSEGU news, Live TV and SSEGU Work areas, contact us or submit a
      job for review. It is written for a Uganda-based service and is intended to be clear about
      what we do and do not promise.
    </p>
    <h2>Information we may receive</h2>
    <p>
      When you browse the site, our hosting and security providers may process technical information
      such as an IP address, browser type, device information, requested pages, approximate timing
      and error records. This information helps deliver, secure and maintain the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email us, we receive the address and information you choose to include. If an employer
      submits a vacancy through SSEGU Work, we may receive organisation details, a contact person,
      contact email, vacancy information, website links and supporting information supplied in the
      form. Please do not include applicant personal data or sensitive information that is not
      needed to review a vacancy.
    </p>
    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>to provide, secure and improve the website and its features;</li>
      <li>to respond to enquiries, corrections, privacy requests and employer follow-up;</li>
      <li>to review, verify, edit and decide whether to publish submitted opportunities;</li>
      <li>to prevent abuse, fraud, malicious activity and technical failures; and</li>
      <li>to meet applicable legal, regulatory or dispute-resolution requirements.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Job submissions and retention</h2>
    <p>
      A job submission is private review material, not an automatic publication request. Accepted
      submissions are retained only as long as reasonably needed for editorial records and the
      publication lifecycle. The current submission notice states that accepted submissions may be
      kept for up to 90 days after review, while rejected or withdrawn records are intended to be
      deleted within 30 days, subject to legal, security or dispute-related needs.
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies, advertising and third parties</h2>
    <p>
      The site may use necessary storage or similar technologies for functionality, security and
      preferences. Advertising, embedded media, live-stream providers, hosting, email and security
      services may process information under their own policies. External links and third-party
      services are not controlled by SSEGU; review their notices before sharing information with
      them. We do not sell personal information as a business practice.
    </p>
    <h2>Choices and requests</h2>
    <p>
      You may contact us to ask what personal information we hold about you, request correction or
      deletion where applicable, or raise a privacy concern. We may need to verify a request and may
      retain limited information where required for security, legal compliance or recordkeeping.
      Contact <a href="mailto:africa.is.so.rich@gmail.com">africa.is.so.rich@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Security and changes</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable administrative and technical measures appropriate to the service, but no
      internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure. We may update
      this notice when the service, law or our practices change; the date above will identify the
      current version.
    </p>
    <p class="prose-note">This notice describes platform practices and is not legal advice.</p>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
